why Every Alliance quest of Razorfen Kraul in one run, lead-ins included.

# Razorfen Kraul's Alliance quests in one guide: the lead-ins (for Warriors and
# Shamans their class chains too), Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet, one run, then
# the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so the guide picks up
# wherever the chain stands.
#
# The quests: Mebok Mizzyrix's 1221 Blueleaf Tubers (with the crate, manual
# and command stick by him); Henrig Lonebrow's Journal (object 19861, Thousand
# Needles) starts 1100 Lonebrow's Journal -> Falfindel Waywarder's 1101 The
# Crone of the Kraul (Razorflank's Medallion); inside, Heralath Fallowbrook's
# 1142 Mortality Wanes (Treshala's Pendant, for Treshala in Darnassus) and
# Willix the Importer's 1144 (an escort). Warriors: Kelv Sternhammer's 1698 ->
# Yorus Barleybrew's 1699 The Rethban Gauntlet -> 1702 -> Furen Longbeard's
# 1701 Fire Hardened Mail (spider fangs in the Wetlands, chimaera horns in
# Stonetalon, Roogug's Vial of Phlogiston). Shamans: Eldrun Stormbreaker's
# 94789 Call of Air -> Veyric Thunderhame's 96264 Elemental Aid (Charlga's
# Tattered Note).
#
# Left out: 79358 Storm, Earth, and Fire, the Shamans' follow-up, whose ender
# in the data (Rau Cliffrunner) is a Horde NPC.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, Heralath or Willix inside, so
# their goals stand at the door (@42.9,90.2, The Barrens) with `group 5`. The
# bosses come in the order of a run of my own (as a Horde character: Death
# Speaker Jargba, Aggem Thorncurse, Overlord Ramtusk, Roogug, Agathelos,
# Charlga Razorflank, then Willix's escort). Every quest goal is counted by the
# quest log, so a group that takes them in another order still gets each step
# ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - A run of my own on 2026-11-11 (Horde, five players, level 31), recorded
#   with Polestar's recorder and shared with Polestar Client: the bosses in the
#   order above, the tubers dug along the way, Willix taken and escorted after
#   Charlga.
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   29 to 38). Several of its quests need level 30, so the guide starts there.
# INGAME: where inside does Heralath Fallowbrook stand?

